  "design": {
    "description": "The single SharedChannel endpoint owner classifies RPC/write expiry against its scan-cached awake timestamp, then uses an internal buffered-poll entry that does not repeat the public exact Clock.now preflight.",
    "public_contract": "Public HTTP/2 and gRPC deadline poll APIs retain exact usableAwake validation. Wrong-clock and already-expired public calls still return Timeout before consuming buffered events.",
    "io_contract": "The owner-only poll never reads the socket. Any WINDOW_UPDATE or other transport output retains the original absolute deadline and executes the ordinary downstream deadline checks."
  },
